The first local S2 implementation used a support-covering syntactic scaffold plus mixed wrapping. The frozen protocol axis is **semantic support/live_k**, not merely syntactic variable occurrence. Post-run audit found that only 55.161% of admitted S2 formulas retained semantic support equal to the requested `live_k` (measured exactly from canonical ANF). Therefore this S2 run is invalid for support-stratified confirmatory claims and is retained here only as superseded audit evidence.

No favorable subgroup from this run is carried forward. The replacement generator is fixed by construction rather than by outcome filtering: `F = parity(x0,...,x{k-1}) XOR h`, where `h` is generated from degree-2 AND atoms under the BASIC operator family. The invariant "no degree-1 ANF monomials in h" is closed under every two-input Boolean operator, so the parity linear terms cannot cancel. This guarantees semantic support exactly `live_k` without selecting cases after observing benchmark outcomes.
